  "Notes": "Bare 300 A aluminium film on a quartz substrate (the unmatched reference for the 1M filter)\nSpecification: Reference: transmittance of the unmatched Al film at 2536 A.\nReported: T = 0.025 at 2536 A for a bare 300 A aluminum film on a quartz substrate, versus 0.65 maximum when properly matched (p. 911-912).\nNotes: Single layer. Uses the constant Al index printed in the Fig. 2 caption (n = 0.18, k = 2.78 at 2536 A), valid only near 253.6 nm. Quartz index not printed: generic SiO2 (n ~ 1.50 at 254 nm). Light incident from air on the film side; normal incidence assumed.\nLayers from Text p. 911-912 and Fig. 2 caption (Al constants 0.18 - i2.78 at 2536 A); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours T 0.0308 at 253.6 nm; paper T 0.025 (p. 911). Aluminium is Rakic’s data; the paper’s ultraviolet constants for evaporated aluminium are not given.",
